    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist in the `POST /api/owners` validation pipeline, whose first step is `ValidateOwnerFields`.\n\nChanges to `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java`:\n\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set: `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`.\n- Extended `normalizeEmail(...)` so that a present email must be both syntactically valid **and** not on the blocklist; otherwise it adds an `\"email\"` error.\n- Added `isDisposableDomain(...)`, which extracts the domain after the last `@` and matches case-insensitively.\n\nAn offending email flows into the existing `OwnerFieldsInvalidException`, whose handler returns **HTTP 400** with body `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}` \u2014 no new YAML or escalation handler was needed. This reuses the established validate-then-reject pattern per AGENTS.md (put validation first so an invalid body is a 400).\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` passes and **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
